PlotJuggler SDK is licensed per-module. Every source file carries an
SPDX-License-Identifier header that is authoritative for that file.

  Module          License        Full text
  ------------    -----------    ---------------
  pj_base         Apache-2.0     LICENSE-APACHE
  pj_plugins      Apache-2.0     LICENSE-APACHE
  examples        Apache-2.0     LICENSE-APACHE

  MIT exceptions (keep their MIT headers):

  pj_base/include/pj_base/agent_tools/            MIT    LICENSE-MIT
  pj_base/src/agent_tools/                        MIT    LICENSE-MIT
  pj_base/tests/agent_tools_series_stats_test.cpp MIT    LICENSE-MIT
  pj_base/tests/derived_recipes_test.cpp          MIT    LICENSE-MIT
  pj_plugins/include/pj_plugins/testing/:
    fake_catalog_host.hpp, fake_multi_dataset_host.hpp,
    fake_object_read_host.hpp, fake_playback_viewport_hosts.hpp,
    fake_plot_tabs_host.hpp, recording_dp_host.hpp MIT  LICENSE-MIT
  pj_plugins/tests/agent_tools_tool_registry_test.cpp
                                                  MIT    LICENSE-MIT

Rationale:

  - The plugin-facing surface (pj_base, pj_plugins) is Apache-2.0 so that
    third parties may build proprietary plugins and applications on top of
    the SDK without restriction. Apache-2.0 also grants an explicit patent
    license to downstream users.

The columnar storage engine (formerly the MPL-2.0 `pj_datastore` module) has
moved to the PlotJuggler application repository. Everything else is
Apache-2.0 except the MIT files listed above (the agent_tools component and
its test fakes).

